Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Access Denied Despite Correct Rule
Symptoms: User should have access but login fails

Solution:

# Check if SSSD cache needs clearing
sudo sss_cache -E

# Restart SSSD service
sudo systemctl restart sssd

# Verify rule syntax
ipa hbacrule-show rulename --all
Issue 2: Rules Not Taking Effect
Symptoms: Changes to rules don't seem to apply

Solution:

# Force SSSD to refresh HBAC rules
sudo sss_cache -r

# Check SSSD configuration
sudo sssctl config-check

# Verify time synchronization
sudo chrony sources -v
Issue 3: Locked Out After Disabling allow_all
Symptoms: Cannot access any systems after disabling default rule

Solution:

# Re-enable allow_all temporarily
ipa hbacrule-enable allow_all

# Create emergency admin access rule
ipa hbacrule-add emergency_admin_access
ipa hbacrule-add-user emergency_admin_access --users=admin
ipa hbacrule-add-service emergency_admin_access --hbacsvcs=sshd
ipa hbacrule-add-host emergency_admin_access --hosts=ipa-server.example.com
Security Best Practices
Principle of Least Privilege
Create specific rules for each role
Avoid overly broad access permissions
Regularly review and audit access rules
Rule Naming Conventions
# Use descriptive names that indicate:
# - Who: user/group type
# - What: service/action
# - Where: host/location

# Good examples:
# dev_ssh_webservers
# dba_sudo_dbservers
# contractor_limited_devhosts
Regular Maintenance
# Create script for regular HBAC rule auditing
cat > /usr/local/bin/hbac-audit.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
echo "=== HBAC Rules Audit ==="
echo "Active Rules:"
ipa hbacrule-find --enabled=true

echo -e "\nDisabled Rules:"
ipa hbacrule-find --enabled=false

echo -e "\nRules without users:"
for rule in $(ipa hbacrule-find --raw | grep "cn:" | cut -d: -f2); do
    if ! ipa hbacrule-show $rule --raw | grep -q "memberuser"; then
        echo "  $rule"
    fi
done
EOF

chmod +x /usr/local/bin/hbac-audit.sh
Verification and Testing
Comprehensive Test Matrix
Create a test matrix to verify all access scenarios:

# Create test script
cat > /usr/local/bin/hbac-test-matrix.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

USERS=("jdeveloper" "msmith" "ccontractor")
HOSTS=("client1.example.com" "client2.example.com")

echo "HBAC Test Matrix Results:"
echo "========================"

for user in "${USERS[@]}"; do
    for host in "${HOSTS[@]}"; do
        echo -n "Testing $user -> $host: "
        result=$(ipa hbactest --user=$user --host=$host --service=sshd 2>/dev/null)
        if echo "$result" | grep -q "Access granted"; then
            echo "ALLOWED"
        else
            echo "DENIED"
        fi
    done
done
EOF

chmod +x /usr/local/bin/hbac-test-matrix.sh
./usr/local/bin/hbac-test-matrix.sh
